                <pb facs="0367" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-14T17:00:00-04:00">September 14, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>248. Since dictating my number 247, September 14, 4 p.m., I have received your
                    No. 270, September 13, midnight, Mr. MacDonald’s criticism of the agreement.
                    This reenforces my suggestion that we <pb facs="0368" n="232" xml:id="pg232"/>
                    allow the publication of that agreement to wait until after Mr. MacDonald’s
                    visit. Assuming that this can be done I will not now attempt any review of Mr.
                    MacDonald’s suggestions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
